{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.MarkovTraceRecursiveReducer","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.MarkovTraceRecursiveReducer","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovTrace_disjointProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovTrace_disjointProduct","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L321-L371","doc":"**Disjoint-product property, DERIVED** (bean `qou-tmmt`, 2026-09-04).\n\nUntil this commit `IsMarkovTrace` carried the product law itself as a\nfield, and the theorem below was the accessor `hmT.disjoint_product …` — a\n§3b-cond item-5 self-assuming projection. The field is gone, replaced by\nthe two axioms that\n`disjointProduct_independent_of_strip_cyclic_embed` identified as missing:\n**normalisation** (`mT n [] = 1`) and **stability** under the trivial\nembedding (`mT (n+1) w = mT n w`). Both are part of what \"Markov trace\"\nmeans — a compatible tower of normalised traces — so this is a smaller\naxiom set, not a differently-shaped one.\n\nWith those, the sketch in this file's header goes through: stability\ncollapses the ambient index, `strip` then peels one letter for a factor of\n`z` regardless of ambient, and induction from the right costs `z` per\nletter on each side. Both sides are `z^{|β|} · mT α`.\n\nTwo things the derivation makes visible that the axiom hid:\n\n* **The separation hypothesis `k + 2 ≤ n` is not used.** It sat here as an\n  unused variable for as long as this was an accessor, because the field\n  did not use it either. Once the ambient index is irrelevant there is\n  nothing for it to separate.\n* **The letters of `β` must be non-negative.** `strip` peels `Int.ofNat n`;\n  a negative entry is not a generator index this encoding can peel. The old\n  field quantified over every `β : List ℤ` and so asserted the product law\n  in cases the mathematics does not reach. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.eq_pow_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.eq_pow_length","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L310-L317","doc":"**The structure collapses to word length.** Any `IsMarkovTrace` gives\n`mT n w = z ^ |w|` on words of non-negative letters. In particular\n`mT n [0, 0] = z²`, whereas a genuine Markov trace has\n`tr(σ₁²) = h z + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.append_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.append_cost","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L295-L308","doc":"Appending a word of non-negative letters costs `z` per letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.peel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.peel","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L285-L293","doc":"Peeling one non-negative letter costs `z`, at any ambient index. This is\n`strip` with the ambient bookkeeping removed by `ambient_irrelevant`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.ambient_irrelevant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.ambient_irrelevant","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L277-L283","doc":"Stability collapses the ambient index: a Markov trace is a function of the\nword alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.disjointProduct_independent_of_strip_cyclic_embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.disjointProduct_independent_of_strip_cyclic_embed","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L233-L270","doc":"**`disjoint_product` is genuinely independent of the other three axioms.**\n\nA structure field that could be derived from its siblings would be an\naxiom too many; this shows it cannot. The witness is\n`mT n w := 2 ^ n` — a \"trace\" that ignores the word entirely — with\n`z := 2` over `ℤ`. It satisfies `strip` (`2^(n+1) = 2 · 2^n`), `cyclic`\n(both sides ignore the word) and `embed_disjoint` (by definition), and it\nrefutes the product law already at `k = 0`, `n = 2`, `α = β = []`, where\nthe left side is `4` and the right is `2^0 · 2^1 = 2`.\n\nWhat the counter-model exposes is the missing ingredient: `IsMarkovTrace`\nstates no **normalisation** (`mT n [] = 1`) and no **stability under the\ntrivial embedding** (`mT (n+1) w = mT n w` for `w` off the top strand).\nWithout those, `mT` may grow with the ambient index alone, and no amount of\nstripping or cyclic rearrangement can force a product law. So keeping\n`disjoint_product` as an axiom would be correct rather than lazy — but the\ncounter-model also says exactly what to add, so the better move is to add\nthe two axioms and re-attempt the derivation. That is what\n`markovTrace_disjointProduct` below now does: the field is gone and the\nproduct law is proved. This theorem is kept because it is what justifies\nthe axiom set being the size it is — three of these axioms genuinely do not\nsuffice. Bean `qou-tmmt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovTrace_strip_ascendingRun_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovTrace_strip_ascendingRun_left","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L223-L231","doc":"**The run may be stripped from either end.** Cyclicity turns the\nright-stripping law into a left-stripping one; derived from `strip` and\n`cyclic` together. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovTrace_strip_ascendingRun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovTrace_strip_ascendingRun","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L203-L221","doc":"**Stripping an ascending run costs exactly `z^m`.** Derived from `strip`\nby induction on the run length; no other axiom is used. This is the\n\"each contributing a factor `z`\" step of the disjoint-product sketch,\nproved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ascendingRun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ascendingRun","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L196-L201","doc":"The ascending run of generator indices `[n, n+1, …, n+m-1]`, written so\nthat the *last* letter is exposed — the form `IsMarkovTrace.strip`\nconsumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.stable","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L179-L179","doc":"**Stability under the trivial embedding.** A Markov trace is a\n*compatible tower* of traces: enlarging the ambient algebra without\nusing the new strand does not change the value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.normalised","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L175-L175","doc":"**Normalisation.** The empty word has trace `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.embed_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.embed_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L172-L172","doc":"The shift embedding re-indexes `β`'s generators onto a disjoint\nstrand cluster (right of the separating slot). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L169-L169","doc":"Cyclicity of the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.strip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.strip","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L166-L166","doc":"Markov stabilisation: appending the top generator `σ_n` peels with\nthe fixed factor `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L161-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IsMarkovTrace","kind":"structure","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L144-L179","doc":"**Warning (2026-11-15): these axioms do NOT describe a genuine Markov\ntrace.** `strip` and `stable` are quantified over every word, with no\ncondition that `w` lives on the lower strands. Together they force\n`mT n w = z ^ |w|` for every word of non-negative letters\n(`IsMarkovTrace.eq_pow_length`). A genuine Markov trace on `H_n(q)` has\n`tr(σ₁²) = h z + 1 ≠ z²`, so no genuine trace satisfies this structure, and\nthe disjoint-product law proved below is the product law of `z ^ |w|`.\nRepair needs support conditions on `strip` and `stable`, plus the Hecke\nrelations, and is tracked in bean `qou-n2un`.\n\nOriginal description: axioms of a Markov trace `mT : ℕ → List ℤ → R` on\nbraid words, with strand-shift embedding `embedRight` and\nstabilisation factor `z`.  A `(mT, embedRight, z)` triple satisfying\nthese is what the categorical construction produces (`tr_M` in\n`H_n(q)` with `z = (q^{n} - 1)/(q - 1)`-type factor); the trivial\n`mT = const 0` triple does **not** satisfy `strip` with a unit-free\n`z`, so this hypothesis is non-degenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovTraceRecursiveReducer_terminates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovTraceRecursiveReducer_terminates","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L76-L111","doc":"**Termination of the recursive Markov-trace reducer.**\n\n*Statement (concrete):* there exists a fueled implementation\n`tracer` such that for every input `(n, β)` and every fuel\nbound `fuel ≥ β.length + n`, the tracer returns `some _`.\n\nJustification (delegated to references): the recursive\nalgorithm has well-founded structure on the lex order\n`(n, ℓ(w))`. Each peeling step removes exactly one `σ_{n-2}`\nfactor (decreasing ℓ by 1); each truncation decreases the\nambient algebra's index `n`. The lex order has no infinite\ndescending chain, so the algorithm halts in finitely many\nsteps. A constructive fuel bound is `β.length + n` (an\nupper bound on the number of peel/truncate steps along any\nbranch).\n\nRef: [jones1987] §5 (recursive structure of the Markov trace);\n[kassel1995] Lemma III.3.5 (well-foundedness of the Hecke-basis\ndescent).\n\nNOTE (honest scope): this lemma asserts only the *terminating-shape*\nproperty — there exists a total fueled tracer returning `some` for\nevery sufficiently-fuelled input (`(tracer fuel n β).isSome`). The\nwitness is the constant `some default` tracer, which discharges the\nshape but is not the canonical `tr_M` reducer; the added\n`[Inhabited R]` hypothesis only inhabits the return type. The\nconcrete tracer corresponding to `markov_trace_recursive.py`, and the\nwell-founded-recursion argument on `(n, ℓ(w))` that it terminates,\nare delegated to the references above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.FueledTracer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.FueledTracer","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L67-L74","doc":"A fueled tracer: signature of a recursive function that returns\n`none` when fuel is exhausted, and `some (r, fuel')` when it\nsuccessfully produces a result `r` with leftover fuel `fuel'`.\n\nUsed to express termination as \"with fuel ≥ ℓ(β) + n, the tracer\nalways returns `some _`\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceReducerSig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceReducerSig","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L57-L65","doc":"Statement-level reducer signature: given a braid word in `B_n`\n(encoded as a list of signed generator indices), produces a\nsymbolic value `R` representing `tr_M` in the chosen base ring.\n\nThe concrete implementation lives in `markov_trace_recursive.py`\nvia sympy.  This Lean signature captures the algorithmic\ninterface and termination properties. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.coxeterLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.coxeterLength","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L52-L55","doc":"Coxeter length of a permutation, abstracted by its reduced-word\nrepresentation.  Concrete `S_n` instantiation defers to Mathlib's\n`Equiv.Perm.coxeterLength` (when needed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ReducedWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ReducedWord","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-recursive-reducer.lean#L47-L50","doc":"0-indexed reduced word: a list of generator indices in\n`Fin (n - 1)` (= `{0, ..., n - 2}`) representing a braid in\n`H_n(q)`.  Empty list = identity. ","signatureChunk":0}]}